<div class="bar"><span>Revert Creations · field guide 02</span><span>Digital order → physical work</span></div>
<header><a class="brand" href="{{ route('home') }}">REVERT CREATIONS</a><a href="{{ route('benchcue.referral', ['source' => 'shopify_production_sheet_guide_header']) }}">BenchCue for Shopify →</a></header>
<main>
    <section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">For engraving, printing, sewing, assembly, and other made-to-order shops</div><h1>Carry the customization—not the whole order.</h1><p class="intro">A Shopify order screen contains everything needed to transact. A production bench needs a smaller artifact: the exact item, quantity, SKU, and public choices that tell someone what to make.</p></div><aside class="sheet" aria-label="Example production sheet"><strong>PRODUCTION<br>SHEET / 0142</strong><dl><dt>Item</dt><dd>Walnut desk plaque</dd><dt>Quantity</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>SKU</dt><dd>PLQ-WAL-8</dd><dt>Engraving</dt><dd>Northline Studio</dd><dt>Finish</dt><dd>Natural oil</dd></dl></aside></section>
    <section class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">The useful data boundary</div><h2>What belongs on the sheet.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Shopify line-item properties are name-and-value pairs attached to a specific item. Themes and customization tools commonly use them for engraving text, monograms, colors, uploaded-file references, and other buyer choices.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Product identity</h3><p>Product and variant title, quantity, and SKU when one exists.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Public customization</h3><p>The visible line-item properties the customer reviewed with the purchase.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Production context</h3><p>An order reference sufficient for the maker to reconcile the finished item.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Nothing ornamental</h3><p>Remove navigation, payment status, marketing panels, and unrelated order detail.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="privacy"><div><div class="eyebrow">A narrower sheet is safer</div><h2>Do not print customer data by habit.</h2></div><div><p>A maker normally does not need a buyer’s email address, phone number, billing details, or full shipping address to engrave a name or select a thread color. Keep those fields in Shopify unless the production step genuinely requires them.</p><ul><li>Treat uploaded references and free-form personalization as customer-provided content.</li><li>Do not turn private or underscore-prefixed workflow metadata into public-facing instructions accidentally.</li><li>Store as little as the production task needs, for no longer than it needs it.</li></ul></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">A repeatable handoff</div><h2>Build the workflow around the artifact.</h2></div><div class="copy workflow"><article class="step"><div><h3>Capture choices at the item</h3><p>Use clear property names such as “Engraving,” “Thread color,” or “Reference file” so the customer and maker read the same instruction.</p></div></article><article class="step"><div><h3>Review before production</h3><p>Confirm the public values are present and usable. A blank or ambiguous choice should stop the item before it reaches the bench.</p></div></article><article class="step"><div><h3>Print one focused sheet</h3><p>Group each item with its own quantity, SKU, and customization values. Preserve line breaks and long values rather than clipping the instruction.</p></div></article><article class="step"><div><h3>Reconcile the finished work</h3><p>Keep the order reference on the sheet so the completed piece can return to fulfillment without carrying unnecessary customer data through the workshop.</p></div></article></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">Manual or app-assisted</div><h2>Choose based on order volume.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>For an occasional personalized order, a handwritten card or carefully edited printout may be enough. <a href="{{ route('benchcue.template') }}">Use the free editable production-sheet template</a> to try the handoff before adding software. If the details belong in the package too, <a href="{{ route('benchcue.packing-slip-guide') }}">use the free Liquid guide</a> or <a href="{{ route('packing-slip-setup', ['source' => 'production-sheet-guide']) }}">buy the $149 packing-slip setup</a> for a block tailored to your field names.</p><p>The moment staff repeatedly copy the same item fields out of Shopify, the handoff becomes a candidate for automation. The standard is not “more software.” It is fewer transcription steps, fewer irrelevant fields at the bench, and an artifact a maker can trust without reopening the entire order.</p></div></section>
    <section class="cta"><div><div class="eyebrow">A focused Shopify admin extension</div><h2>BenchCue makes the sheet.</h2><p>BenchCue pulls the item, quantity, SKU, and public customization choices into a maker-ready production sheet. It is $7 monthly with a seven-day trial. Shopify App Store review is currently pending, so the public page shows the workflow without pretending installation is available yet.</p></div><a class="button" href="{{ route('benchcue.referral', ['source' => 'shopify_production_sheet_guide_cta']) }}">See the BenchCue workflow →</a></section>
</main>
